  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Ingest and typing",
      "items": [
        "One adapter per source format, each with a field-level fixture test",
        "The alphabet is a reviewed artefact: typing, redaction and outcome rules live in YAML, never in code",
        "Redaction happens at ingestion, so no free text reaches a stored artefact"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Mining",
      "items": [
        "Four obligation patterns plus recommendations, each declaring the window it is measured over",
        "Provenance says whether the evidence is the operator's own, borrowed, or absent — an absent verdict is a refusal, and it is kept",
        "Contradictions, then subsumption, then vacuity: a verdict naming another rule outranks 'uninformative'"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Serving and measurement",
      "items": [
        "Rule identity is stable across runs, so a verdict given last week still applies to the rule mined today",
        "The advisor abstains on an unknown fact rather than assuming it false, and serves only what a person adjudicated real",
        "Evaluate and diff are the only modules that may read a policy; a build check enforces it"
      ]
    }
  ]
